      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this bright and spacious one-bedroom ground floor apartment to the market in the ever-popular Lanesborough development, Finglas, Dublin 11.\n\nNo. 63 comes to the market in good condition throughout and offers exceptionally spacious living accommodation extending to c. 68 sq. m. The property benefits from its own door entrance and is sure to appeal to first-time buyers, investors and anyone looking to downsize.\n\nThe location is highly convenient with Charlestown Shopping Centre and a wide range of shops, cafés, schools and recreational amenities all within easy reach. Dublin Airport, Dublin City Centre and DCU are also easily accessible, while the M50 and M1 motorway networks are only minutes away. The area is well serviced by public transport with several bus routes nearby.\n\nBright and well laid out internal living accommodation of c. 68 sq. m. comprises of entrance hallway, spacious open-plan living/dining area, fitted kitchen, large double bedroom with fitted wardrobes and bathroom with bath and shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nThe living area is particularly generous and benefits from an abundance of natural light, timber flooring and feature fireplace. The fitted kitchen comes with ample storage, integrated oven and electric hob. The large double bedroom provides excellent space along with fitted wardrobes and direct access to a private outdoor terrace.\n\nAdditional benefits include gas fired central heating, double glazed windows, own door entrance and one designated parking space.\n\nNo. 63 represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a spacious one-bedroom apartment in a well-established and highly convenient location. Early viewing is highly advised, contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 086 832 3302 or 01 541 1455 to arrange a viewing.\n\nKey Features\n• c. 68 sq. m.\n• BER C\n• Built c. 2004\n• Own door entrance\n• Good condition throughout\n• Exceptionally spacious living accommodation\n• Bright open-plan living/dining area\n• Feature fireplace\n• Fitted kitchen\n• Integrated oven & electric hob\n• Large double bedroom\n• Fitted wardrobes\n• Private outdoor terrace\n• Gas fired central heating\n• Double glazed windows\n• One designated parking space\n• Management fees c. 1,200 per annum\n• Close to Charlestown Shopping Centre\n• Easy access to M50, M1 and Dublin Airport\n• Well serviced by public transport\n• Ideal for first-time buyers, investors, and downsizers\n• Early viewing highly advised"
      },
      {
